Suppose $\gL$ is the generator of a Markov process $(x_t)_{t \in [0, T]}$ with path measure $\P$, $h$ is a strictly positive function, and $\lambda$ is an arbitrary function. Then the transformed process with the generator $\gL^{h, \lambda}$, defined as
    \begin{equation*}
        \gL^{h, \lambda} f = h^{-1} \gL(h f) - \lambda f,
    \end{equation*}
    is another a Markov process

there exists a probability measure $\sQ$ absolutely continuous to the original probability measure $\P$ with the Radon-Nikodym derivative satisfying that
